      "id": "7a1b2c3d-4e5f-4061-8273-849506a1b2c3",
      "name": "HTTP - Get Thread Original Message",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        -2416,
        400
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "gmailOAuth2": {
          "id": "K0aEhfZvTx9f7hTm",
          "name": "Gmail account"
        }
      },
      "notes": "Every message in a Gmail thread shares the same thread_id, including the original outbound one - fetching the whole thread and reading messages[0] (the thread root) resolves the right client regardless of how many reply-hops deep the current message is. Deliberately not using In-Reply-To/rfc822msgid search here: that only points at the immediate parent, so a lead replying to their own prior reply (not the original) would walk back one hop to a message that never had the custom header set, and incorrectly fall back."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const base = $('CODE - Normalize Reply Email').first().json;\nconst response = $json;\n\nlet clientType = '';\nlet sheetId = '';\nconst firstMessage = response && Array.isArray(response.messages) && response.messages[0];\nif (firstMessage && firstMessage.payload && Array.isArray(firstMessage.payload.headers)) {\n  const getHeader = (name) => (firstMessage.payload.headers.find((h) => h.name.toLowerCase() === name.toLowerCase()) || {}).value || '';\n  clientType = getHeader('X-Client-Type');\n  sheetId = getHeader('X-Client-Sheet-Id');\n}\n\n// Falls back to the root template/ops spreadsheet whenever the thread root can't be resolved\n// (thread lookup failed, or the header is missing - e.g. it predates this feature shipping).\n// GS - Lookup Lead by Email will then correctly find no match there, and the existing\n// unmatched-reply handling (GS - Log Unmatched Reply) takes over from that point on.\nconst ROOT_FALLBACK_SHEET_ID = '1P9gpsLp0PKTV8PN9kQ-0E-6qy_ZQStmnJbh7ehtiu6M';\n\nreturn [{ json: {\n  ...base,\n  resolved_client_type: clientType,\n  sheet_id: sheetId || ROOT_FALLBACK_SHEET_ID\n} }];"
      },
